# Cursor Rules for Tysonpe — Permanent Design & Quality Directive

You are pair programming on Tysonpe, an elite creator commerce and fintech platform for India.
You must adhere to the core memory rules defined in CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, and DESIGN.md:

1. ANTI-AI SLOP (Taste Skill):
   - NO purple/indigo radial blur circles behind hero text.
   - NO generic centered 3-card or 5-card feature grids with colorful icons.
   - NO emojis as primary UI icons (always import bespoke SVGs from src/components/gateway-icons.tsx).
   - NO uniform, cadence-less padding (p-6 everywhere). Use deliberate visual hierarchy.
   - NO generic placeholder claims. Use real currency (₹), GST rates, and settlement times.

2. TYPOGRAPHY & DESIGN TOKENS (UI UX Pro Max):
   - Headings: Plus Jakarta Sans (--font-display aliases --font-sans) with tight tracking (-0.025em).
   - Body & Numbers: Plus Jakarta Sans (--font-sans) with tabular-nums for financial figures.
   - Semantic tokens: --bg (#ffffff), --surface, --surface-2, --ink, --line, --brand (#4f46e5), --good (#10b981).

3. MOTION & MICRO-INTERACTIONS (Design Motion Principles & Design Spells):
   - Transitions: 150ms for buttons/hover, 220ms for modals/drawers. Easing: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1).
   - Micro-interactions: active:scale-[0.98] on buttons, tactile feedback on status changes.
   - Respect prefers-reduced-motion.

4. UI COMPONENT ARCHITECTURES:
   - Skiper UI: Clean segmented controls, interactive cards, minimal border shines.
   - Animaster Lib: Layered elevation, fluid glass surfaces (backdrop-blur-md).
   - Vengeance UI: Micro-interaction cards, subtle perspective borders.

5. VERIFICATION:
   - Always run `npm test` before declaring code ready.
